            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">20. How colspan Works</h2>

            <p>
                When you use <code>colspan="3"</code>, the cell takes the
                horizontal space of three normal cells.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;tr&gt;

    &lt;td colspan="3"&gt;
        One cell across three columns
    &lt;/td&gt;

&lt;/tr&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
    <button type="button"
            class="try-it-btn"
            onclick="tryHTML(this)">
        Try It
    </button>
</div>

            <div class="example-box">
                <strong>Concept:</strong>

                <table class="demo-table">
                    <tr>
                        <td colspan="3">One Cell Across Three Columns</td>
                    </tr>
                </table>
            </div>

            <h2 class="h3 fw-bold mt-5">21. How rowspan Works</h2>

            <p>
                When you use <code>rowspan="3"</code>, the cell takes the
                vertical space of three normal cells.
            </p>

            <pre><code>&lt;tr&gt;

    &lt;td rowspan="3"&gt;
        One cell across three rows
    &lt;/td&gt;

    &lt;td&gt;Row 1&lt;/td&gt;

&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Row 2&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;

&lt;tr&gt;
    &lt;td&gt;Row 3&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;</code></pre>

<div class="try-it-container">
